# RawEval Monorepo Cursor Rules

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

**Turborepo monorepo** with Next.js apps and shared packages following **feature-based architecture**.

### Structure:
```
apps/
  ├── landing/      # www.raweval.com (public landing page)
  ├── chat/         # chat.raweval.com (user chatbot interface)
  ├── experts/      # experts.raweval.com (expert workbench)
  └── admin/        # admin.raweval.com (internal admin/org dashboard)

packages/
  ├── ui/           # Shared Shadcn UI components
  ├── types/        # Shared TypeScript types
  ├── utils/        # Shared utilities
  ├── config/       # Shared configs (tsconfig, eslint, prettier, tailwind)
  ├── auth/         # Authentication & RBAC
  └── db/           # Database client & schema
```

**See also:**
- `.cursorrules.shadcn.md` - Shadcn MCP server optimization
- `.cursorrules.architecture.md` - Detailed architecture patterns

---

## 🚨 CRITICAL RULES - NEVER VIOLATE

### 1. **Cyclic Dependency Prevention (STRICT)**

**ALLOWED Dependency Flow:**
```
apps/* → packages/* (✅ Apps can import from packages)
packages/ui → packages/utils, packages/types (✅ UI can use utils/types)
packages/utils → packages/types (✅ Utils can use types)
packages/auth → packages/types (✅ Auth can use types)
packages/db → packages/types (✅ DB can use types)
```

**FORBIDDEN:**
```
❌ packages/* → apps/*           (Packages NEVER import from apps)
❌ apps/chat → apps/landing       (Apps NEVER import from other apps)
❌ packages/types → packages/*   (Types should have no dependencies)
❌ packages/auth → packages/db    (Auth should not depend on DB)
❌ Circular imports between any two packages
```

**Validation:**
- Before any import, verify the dependency direction
- If you need shared code between apps, move it to `packages/`
- If you need to share between packages, ensure it flows down the hierarchy

---

### 2. **Import Path Rules**

**Workspace Packages (use `@raweval/*`):**
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { Button } from '@raweval/ui/button';
import { cn } from '@raweval/utils';
import type { User, Expert } from '@raweval/types';
import { hasPermission } from '@raweval/auth';
import { db } from '@raweval/db';

// ❌ WRONG
import { Button } from '../../../packages/ui/src/button';
import { Button } from 'packages/ui';
import { Button, Card } from '@raweval/ui'; // No barrel imports!
```

**Internal Imports (use `@/`):**
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Within same app
import { ChatMessage } from '@/features/chat/components/chat-message';
import { chatService } from '@/services/chat-service';
import { Header } from '@/components/layout/header';

// ❌ WRONG
import { ChatMessage } from '../features/chat/components/chat-message';
```

---

### 3. **Feature-Based Architecture (CRITICAL)**

**App Structure:**
```
apps/chat/
├── app/                    # Next.js App Router
│   ├── (public)/          # Route groups (no auth)
│   ├── (tenant)/          # Route groups (auth required)
│   └── api/               # API routes
├── features/               # Feature modules
│   ├── chat/
│   │   ├── components/     # Feature-specific components
│   │   ├── hooks/         # Feature-specific hooks
│   │   ├── services.ts    # Feature business logic
│   │   └── types.ts       # Feature types
│   ├── auth/
│   └── workspace/
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                # Re-export shadcn (app-specific overrides)
│   ├── shared/            # Cross-feature components
│   ├── layout/            # Layout components
│   └── providers/        # Context providers
├── services/              # Business logic layer
├── hooks/                 # Shared hooks
├── lib/                   # App-specific utilities
└── middleware.ts         # Auth & routing middleware
```

**Rules:**
- ✅ Organize by **feature**, not by layer
- ✅ Feature components in `features/*/components/`
- ✅ Business logic in `services/` or `features/*/services.ts`
- ✅ Shared components in `components/shared/` or `components/layout/`
- ❌ Don't create `components/chat/` - use `features/chat/components/`

---

### 4. **Shadcn UI with MCP Server (OPTIMIZED)**

**When using Shadcn MCP Server:**

**✅ CORRECT Workflow:**
1. Use MCP server to add components to `packages/ui/src/`
2. Components are automatically exported with direct paths
3. Import directly: `import { Button } from '@raweval/ui/button'`
4. Never edit generated shadcn components directly in `packages/ui`

**Component Location:**
```
packages/ui/src/
├── button.tsx          # Shadcn component (DO NOT EDIT)
├── card.tsx            # Shadcn component (DO NOT EDIT)
└── ...
```

**App-Specific Overrides:**
```
apps/chat/components/ui/
└── index.ts            # Re-export with app-specific overrides if needed
```

**Rules:**
- ✅ All shadcn components go in `packages/ui/src/`
- ✅ Each component is a separate file (no barrel exports)
- ✅ Use MCP server to add new components
- ✅ If you need to customize, create wrapper in `features/*/components/`
- ❌ Never edit `packages/ui/src/*` components directly
- ❌ Never create barrel exports in `packages/ui`

**MCP Server Commands:**
- Use MCP server to add components: "Add shadcn button component"
- Components are automatically placed in `packages/ui/src/`
- Import path is automatically `@raweval/ui/button`

**See `.cursorrules.shadcn.md` for detailed shadcn rules.**

---

### 5. **Package Creation Rules**

**When to create a new package:**
- ✅ Component is used in 2+ apps
- ✅ Utility function is shared across apps
- ✅ Type definition is shared
- ✅ Configuration is common
- ✅ Business logic is shared (auth, db)

**When NOT to create a package:**
- ❌ Only used in one app (keep it in `features/` or `services/`)
- ❌ App-specific business logic (keep in app's `services/`)
- ❌ One-off utilities (keep in app's `lib/`)

---

### 6. **TypeScript Strictness**

**All packages and apps MUST:**
```json
{
  "strict": true,
  "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
  "noImplicitOverride": true,
  "noUnusedLocals": true,
  "noUnusedParameters": true
}
```

**Type Safety Rules:**
- ✅ Always export types from `packages/types`
- ✅ Use `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/primitives
- ✅ Prefer `unknown` over `any`
- ✅ Use generics for reusable components
- ❌ Never use `any` (use `unknown` instead)
- ❌ Never use `@ts-ignore` (use `@ts-expect-error` with comment)

---

### 7. **Component Organization**

**Hierarchy:**
1. **`packages/ui/src/`**: Shadcn components (generated, don't edit)
2. **`components/ui/`**: Re-export shadcn (app-specific overrides)
3. **`components/shared/`**: Cross-feature components (logo, empty-state)
4. **`components/layout/`**: Layout components (header, sidebar, breadcrumbs)
5. **`components/providers/`**: Context providers
6. **`features/*/components/`**: Feature-specific components

**Rules:**
- ✅ Feature components in `features/*/components/`
- ✅ Shared components in `components/shared/`
- ✅ Layout components in `components/layout/`
- ❌ Don't create `components/chat/` - use `features/chat/components/`

---

### 8. **Services Layer**

**Business Logic Separation:**
```
apps/chat/services/
├── chat-service.ts      # Chat business logic
├── auth-service.ts      # Auth business logic (if app-specific)
└── workspace-service.ts # Workspace business logic
```

**Rules:**
- ✅ Business logic in `services/` or `features/*/services.ts`
- ✅ Services are testable in isolation
- ✅ Services are reusable across components
- ❌ Don't put business logic in components
- ❌ Don't put business logic in hooks (hooks call services)

**Usage:**
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { chatService } from '@/services/chat-service';
await chatService.sendMessage(sessionId, message);

// ❌ WRONG - Business logic in component
const sendMessage = async () => {
  await fetch('/api/chat', { ... }); // Move to service
};
```

---

### 9. **Authentication & Authorization**

**Package: `@raweval/auth`**

**Usage:**
```typescript
import { hasPermission, getSession, requireSession } from '@raweval/auth';
import type { Permission, UserRole } from '@raweval/types';

// Check permissions
if (hasPermission('admin', 'admin:view')) {
  // Show admin panel
}

// Get session (server component)
const session = await getSession();
if (!session) redirect('/login');

// Require session (throws if not authenticated)
const session = await requireSession();
```

**Rules:**
- ✅ Use `@raweval/auth` for RBAC
- ✅ Check permissions in middleware or server components
- ✅ Use `getSession()` in server components
- ❌ Don't implement auth logic in apps (use package)

---

### 10. **Database Access**

**Package: `@raweval/db`**

**Usage:**
```typescript
import { db } from '@raweval/db';

// Use database (after setup)
const users = await db.user.findMany();
```

**Rules:**
- ✅ All database access through `@raweval/db`
- ✅ Database logic in services, not components
- ✅ Use types from `@raweval/types`
- ❌ Don't create database clients in apps

---

### 11. **Route Groups & Middleware**

**Route Groups:**
```
app/
├── (public)/          # Public routes (no auth)
│   ├── login/
│   ├── signup/
│   └── page.tsx
├── (tenant)/         # Tenant-scoped routes (auth required)
│   └── [workspaceSlug]/
│       ├── chat/
│       ├── settings/
│       └── billing/
└── api/              # API routes
```

**Middleware:**
- ✅ Use `middleware.ts` for auth checks
- ✅ Use route groups for organization
- ✅ Protect routes in middleware, not components

**See `.cursorrules.architecture.md` for detailed patterns.**

---

### 12. **Styling & Design Consistency**

**Tailwind:**
- Shared config in `packages/config/tailwind`
- All apps extend the base config
- Custom theme tokens defined once in base config
- Never override core colors per-app

**Global CSS:**
- Base styles in `packages/config/global.css`
- Apps import and extend with app-specific styles only
- Animations defined in base config

**Component Variants:**
- Use `class-variance-authority` (cva) for component variants
- Define variants in the component, not in apps

---

### 13. **Data Fetching & API**

**Types First:**
```typescript
// 1. Define types in packages/types
export interface Expert {
  id: string;
  tier: 1 | 2 | 3;
  name: string;
}

// 2. Use in apps
import type { Expert } from '@raweval/types';

async function getExpert(id: string): Promise<Expert> {
  // ...
}
```

**API Routes:**
- Each app has its own API routes in `app/api/`
- Shared types for request/response
- Use `packages/types` for API contracts
- Business logic in services, not API routes

---

## 📦 Package-Specific Rules

### `packages/ui`
- ✅ Only React components (shadcn generated)
- ✅ Each component in separate file
- ✅ Direct exports: `@raweval/ui/button`
- ❌ No business logic
- ❌ No data fetching
- ❌ No barrel exports
- ❌ Don't edit generated components directly

### `packages/types`
- ✅ Pure TypeScript types/interfaces
- ✅ No runtime code
- ✅ No dependencies (except type-only imports)
- ✅ Export everything explicitly (no `export *`)

### `packages/utils`
- ✅ Pure functions only
- ✅ Fully tested (100% coverage goal)
- ✅ No side effects
- ✅ No React-specific code
- ✅ Each utility in separate file

### `packages/config`
- ✅ Configuration only
- ✅ No runtime code
- ✅ Extend, don't override in apps

### `packages/auth`
- ✅ RBAC and session management
- ✅ Can depend on `@raweval/types`
- ❌ Cannot depend on `@raweval/db`
- ✅ Use in middleware and server components

### `packages/db`
- ✅ Database client and schema
- ✅ Can depend on `@raweval/types`
- ❌ Cannot depend on other packages
- ✅ Use in services, not components

---

## 🚀 Quick Commands Reference

**⚠️ IMPORTANT: Only pnpm is allowed in this monorepo!**
- ❌ `npm install` - FORBIDDEN
- ❌ `yarn install` - FORBIDDEN
- ✅ `pnpm install` - ONLY THIS WORKS

```bash
# Install dependencies
pnpm install

# Dev mode (all apps)
pnpm dev

# Dev mode (specific app)
pnpm --filter @raweval/chat dev

# Build all
pnpm build

# Build specific app
pnpm --filter @raweval/landing build

# Add dependency to app
pnpm --filter @raweval/chat add axios

# Add dependency to package
pnpm --filter @raweval/ui add lucide-react

# Add dependency to root (dev tools)
pnpm add -Dw turbo

# Format all
pnpm format

# Lint all
pnpm lint

# Type check all
pnpm typecheck

# Clean all builds
pnpm clean
```

---

## ✅ Before Every Commit Checklist

- [ ] No cyclic dependencies introduced
- [ ] Imports use correct paths (`@raweval/*`, `@/`)
- [ ] Types exported from `packages/types`
- [ ] Shared components in `packages/ui`
- [ ] Feature components in `features/*/components/`
- [ ] Business logic in `services/`
- [ ] Code formatted (Prettier)
- [ ] No linting errors
- [ ] No TypeScript errors
- [ ] Build succeeds (`pnpm build`)
- [ ] Commit message follows convention

---

## 🆘 Common Issues & Solutions

### Issue: "Cannot find module '@raweval/ui'"
**Solution:** Run `pnpm install` at root to link workspace packages

### Issue: "Circular dependency detected"
**Solution:** Check import direction, move shared code to packages

### Issue: "Type errors in app after package change"
**Solution:** Rebuild packages first: `pnpm --filter '@raweval/*' build`

### Issue: "Slow dev server"
**Solution:** Use `pnpm --filter <app> dev` to run only one app

### Issue: "Vercel build fails"
**Solution:** Check `turbo.json` pipeline and app's `package.json` build script

### Issue: "Shadcn component not found"
**Solution:** Use MCP server to add component, it will be placed in `packages/ui/src/`

